# Generated artifacts.
# `output/` IS committed: it holds the generated results a use case is about,
# and later use cases consume them as input. Keep committed samples small.
# Disposable generated code and scratch artifacts go to `build/` or `dist/`
# instead - never committed, always regenerable from the documented command.
build/
*/build/
dist/
*/dist/

# Slides (Slidev). `public/img/` is generated by slides/scripts/sync_assets.mjs
# from the screenshots already committed in the use-case `input/` folders --
# never a second copy in git. `.slidev/` is Slidev's local cache.
slides/public/img/
.slidev/

# Source data whose licence could not be established.
# `opensearch/input/airports.json` is an export from an existing feature class
# in an Enterprise Geodatabase, handed over without a licence statement. It is
# probably the FAA-derived airports data set, but "probably" is not a licence
# (CLAUDE.md section 3), and this repository is published under CC BY 4.0
# (section 11). The file therefore never enters git. What was taken from it is
# its *structure* - field names, Esri field types, spatial reference, and the
# measured shape of its quirks - which `opensearch/scripts/make_airports_fixture.py`
# rebuilds with synthetic values. Ignored rather than merely untracked, because
# the surrounding `input/` folder is committed in full and a `git add
# opensearch/input` would otherwise take it along.
opensearch/input/airports.json

# Corporate PowerPoint master (`con terra_Folienmaster_en.potx`). Company
# template, not ours to publish under CC BY - the Slidev deck only imitates its
# palette and typography, which are not the file. Never committed.
slides/input/
